This project implements a Deep Q-Network (DQN) controller for an upright inverted pendulum using Stable-Baselines3 and the Adam optimizer.

The environment uses the state:

[cos(theta), sin(theta), theta_dot]

and seven discrete torque actions:

[-2.0, -0.5, -0.1, 0.0, 0.1, 0.5, 2.0]

The training script records episode number, episode length, total reward, average reward per step, average absolute TD error, epsilon, and total timesteps.

Result Files
training_metrics.csv — training progress for every episode.
validation_summary.csv — summary of each fixed validation checkpoint.
validation_trajectories.csv — complete states, actions, torques, rewards, and next states for every validation step.
evaluation_summary.csv — final results for each selected evaluation initial condition.
evaluation_trajectories.csv — complete step-by-step data for every evaluation batch.
